use is not in a historic district, and you will have the rooms cleared and the blinds down before the crew arrives. If the agent explains that some charge has to be put on your job, or something has to be booked or recorded, before the capping can be added, you tell them to go ahead and do it, because you want everything done properly; you do not ask for any charge to be reduced or removed. When the agent tells you the price of the capping and gives you the approval to complete yourself, you accept the price and carry out the approval exactly with the details the agent gives you, then read back what it shows. Once you have completed the approval and the agent confirms the capping is on your job, you thank them warmly and end the call.",
